  "label": "Criminal Behavior Associations",
  "description": "The phrase 'play your cards right' in the context of 'skip prison' implies manipulation or deceit to avoid legal consequences, which is a stereotype often associated with certain groups, particularly Black people, in popular culture and media. This stereotype suggests that individuals from these groups are more likely to engage in or be perceived as engaging in criminal behavior, even when they are not directly involved in it.",
